VXNlcjoxNDY4NzA3MjUxNDgxNDIzODgw', 'rest_id': '1468707251481423880', 'affiliates_highlighted_label': {}, 'has_graduated_access': True, 'is_blue_verified': True, 'profile_image_shape': 'Circle', 'legacy': {'can_dm': True, 'can_media_tag': True, 'created_at': 'Wed Dec 08 22:21:33 +0000 2021', 'default_profile': True, 'default_profile_image': False, 'description': "Freedom Convoy 22' Volunteer. If you don’t help stand against political persecution, you could be next. Author: https://t.co/Vh7oYb3lY4. Engaged @JoannaM441303", 'entities': {'description': {'urls': [{'display_url': 'a.co/d/iReq2dR', 'expanded_url': 'https://a.co/d/iReq2dR', 'url': 'https://t.co/Vh7oYb3lY4', 'indices': [112, 135]}]}, 'url': {'urls': [{'display_url': 'usetoto.com', 'expanded_url': 'https://www.usetoto.com', 'url': 'https://t.co/2vuIMVGprn', 'indices': [0, 23]}]}}, 'fast_followers_count': 0, 'favourites_count': 83903, 'followers_count': 90716, 'friends_count': 4744, 'has_custom_timelines': True, 'is_translator': False, 'listed_count': 197, 'location': 'Ontario, CA', 'media_count': 1428, 'name': 'Tom Marazzo - Author', 'normal_followers_count': 90716, 'pinned_tweet_ids_str': ['1955309763530465567'], 'possibly_sensitive': False, 'profile_banner_url': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_banners/1468707251481423880/1746556087', 'profile_image_url_https': 'https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1958006488082927616/vLhgSZQW_normal.jpg', 'profile_interstitial_type': '', 'screen_name': 'TomMarazzo', 'statuses_count': 21334, 'translator_type': 'none', 'url': 'https://t.co/2vuIMVGprn', 'verified': False, 'want_retweets': False, 'withheld_in_countries': []}, 'professional': {'rest_id': '1692834470506680705', 'professional_type': 'Creator', 'category': [{'id': 957, 'name': 'Author', 'icon_name': 'IconBriefcaseStroke'}]}}}}, 'unmention_data': {}, 'edit_control': {'edit_tweet_ids': ['1876310858407505943'], 'editable_until_msecs': '1736185943000', 'is_edit_eligible': True, 'edits_remaining': '5'}, 'is_translatable': False, 'views': {'count': '72448', 'state': 'EnabledWithCount'}, 'source': '<a href="https://mobile.twitter.com" rel="nofollow">Twitter Web App</a>', 'note_tweet': {'is_expandable': True, 'note_tweet_results': {'result': {'id': 'Tm90ZVR3ZWV0OjE4NzYzMTA4NTgyNTIzODYzMDQ=', 'text': 'Can Parliament hold a vote of no confidence and force an election during prorogation? No. And that’s exactly why Trudeau has done it.\n\nProrogation suspends Parliament entirely. The House of Commons is not in session, meaning MPs cannot debate, pass laws, or hold a confidence vote. No sittings, no votes, no accountability. Trudeau has effectively shielded his government from being removed until Parliament resumes on March 24, 2025.\n\nCould the Governor General (GG) step in and recall Parliament early? Technically, yes. But in practice, this almost never happens unless there’s a major constitutional crisis—like a government losing confidence before prorogation and refusing to step down. That’s not the case here. Unless Trudeau willingly recalls Parliament, we are stuck.\n\nSo what can be done?\n\nMass Political Pressure – The opposition, media, and public could push for an early recall.\nGG Recall (Unlikely) – If the government’s legitimacy completely collapses, the GG could intervene.\nWait for Parliament to Resume – Once Parliament is back, the opposition can immediately introduce a motion of no confidence to try and force an election.\nBut until then, Trudeau has locked his government in place to avoid being removed. That’s the real reason for prorogation.\n\nIt’s not about a leadership race—it’s about denying Canadians a choice. They just assume we’re too stupid to notice. That’s why local and provincial politics should be our focus—the federal government only exists to play these dirty tricks and remind us how much they despise us.', 'entity_set': {'hashtags': [], 'symbols': [], 'urls': [], 'user_mentions': []}, 'richtext': {'richtext_tags': [{'from_index': 1388, 'to_index': 1448, '